FastRDServer
============

This is an UNOFFICIAL fork of rustdesk-server (the open-source edition).
It is NOT affiliated with, endorsed by, or supported by RustDesk or Purslane Ltd.
"RustDesk" is a trademark of Purslane Ltd.

Upstream:  https://github.com/rustdesk/rustdesk-server
Baseline:  1.1.17
License:   GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 (unchanged from upstream)

Modifications made in this fork (summary; see README.md for detail):

  * User accounts: user/user_token tables, argon2id13 password hashing,
    an HTTP API for login, address-book sync and self-service password change.
    Login payloads are sealed with libsodium sealed boxes.
  * Devices bind to an account; the device roster is filtered by group.
  * Same-account devices reach each other without a password; the decision is
    made server-side and carried on the punch-hole/relay messages.
  * A device-enumeration request added to the rendezvous protocol, with a
    mandatory server-key check.
  * RegisterPk carries hostname and platform so rosters are readable.
  * Admin CLI extended: user add/passwd/disable/enable/list, and
    bind/unbind/devices for assigning devices to accounts.
  * Binaries renamed: hbbs -> FastRDServer, hbbr -> FastRDRelay,
    rustdesk-utils -> FastRDServer-utils.

